expanded_source_wording_tex:
\label{def:history-space}
Let \(\sigma\) be a computational substrate and let \(L\) be
an autonomous lift on \(\sigma\).  The \emph{history space}
\(H_{\sigma}^{L}\) is the finite typed set of bounded polynomial-time
computation histories generated by \(L\) on \(\sigma\).  Each
history \(h\inH_{\sigma}^{L}\) records:
\begin{enumerate}
  \item the substrate input instance;
  \item the solver-prefix trace generated under \(L\);
  \item the autonomous-lift internal-state record \(\sigma_{L}(h)\);
  \item the declared predictive continuations available from \(h\);
  \item the audit bookkeeping attached to \(h\).
\end{enumerate}

